    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d753">

                <pb facs="0808" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5068: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-20T12:00:00+08:00">April 20,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received April 20—5 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The following telegram has been sent to American Consul at Geneva: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“April 20, 11 a.m. For the Secretary. Your April 18, 11 p.m.<anchor
                                n="74" xml:id="d753-f1"/> I concur in colleagues’ views as set forth
                            in Shanghai’s April 19, 3 p.m., to Geneva.”<anchor n="75"
                                xml:id="d753-f2"/></p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d753-f1" n="74" xml:id="d753-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 82, April 18, midnight, from the Minister in Switzerland, <ref
                        target="#pg697">p. 697</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d753-f2" n="75" xml:id="d753-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 88, April 23, 2 p.m., from the Minister in Switzerland, <ref
                        target="#pg721">p. 721</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
